                              FileLister v1.2
                              ---------------

 A quite simple-to-use filelister, that allows the SysOp to decide which
 areas to include, how old files to include to make nice lists for the
 users to DL. Handles the most extra-long desc's generated by different
 file_id-handlers.


                                Disclaimer
                                ----------

 This tool is supposed to generate filelists..If it doesn't and instead
 fuck's up your system, I'm not going to take any responsibility.
 
 Further more, the archive can be repacked with any packer, you may add
 as many BBS-add's as you want as long as the following files are included:

  FileList     --> the executable
  FileList.doc --> this doc-file 
  Lister.cfg   --> the example configurarion file
  File_id.diz  --> My nice description! :)


                    How to Install, and configure etc..
                    -----------------------------------

 It's installed as an ordinary CNet C-pfile, but the smartest thing, 
 should be to run it as an event, and thereby get nice and fresh
 filelists for your users!

 The config files should be in 'Sysdata:' and have the name Lister.cfg.
 It's build up like this:

  @BEGIN_FILE_LIST , @END_FILE_LIST : this to lines indicates the end
  and beginning of a new list.

  @END_CFG must be the last thing in your cfg-file, indicating
  the end of the config! (no shit! :) )

  #pack = lha -q a %d %s : this is the line actually executed when 
  the list is complete. %s is the sourcefile, and %d is the destination.
  the source is deleted before the packstring is executed. 

  #pack = copy %s %d

  Will copy the source til the destination, just like that.

  #source = ram:MainMonthly.RD : this is the name, and the path to the
  source-file. This file will be deleted after the packstring has been
  executed.

  #dest = gfiles:listor/MainMonthly.LhA : This is the name and the path
  of the destination. I.E the result will have name in be in tha path 
  specified here. The file will be deleted BEFORE executing the packstring.
  Thus removing old redundant filelists.

  #tempdir = ram: : Specifies the path to temporaryfiles. This must be 
  specified in all seperate filelists. (I.E after every @BEGIN..)
  If not specified, raM: will be used.

  #header = s:myheader.txt : This adds the file myheader.txt as a header
  (suprise!) to your filelist. Once defined it'll be added to ALL following
  lists or until re-defined.
  
  #footer = s:myfooter.txt : This adds the file myfooter.txt as a footer 
  to your filelist. It'll behave just like the #header-option.
  Thus means, in the example-cfg, the first list'll have the myfooter.txt
  added to it. the second list'll get both the footer AND the headerfile
  added! If you don't wan't any header/footer at all, just skip this part.

  #date = : this line set's how old files that should be included in the
  list, 'NULL' includes ALL files, 7 skips files older than 7 days, 

  #liststyle = 0/1 : Different styles for the listing, i.e 
  liststyle = 1, will, for example, add the file-number, the file name
  up to 19 chars, if name is longer than 19, the 19 first chars + a '*'
  will be added, the filesize in bytes,the date in the format mm-dd-yy,
  number of downloads and description.
  At the end of the list, the total number of files, and bytes in the area
  will be printed!

  ex:

===============================================================================
Listing of subboard TXT-files:
===============================================================================

  49 a-pro1.LHA                5593              24-11-95                    0
                                  NEW SWEDISH MAGAZINE - Amiga-Pro first issue
                                  Contains: cool Amiga products and general   
                                  Amiga news. DON'T MISS THIS!!               


  Files in area: 1
  Bytes in area: 5593

end ex.

  lisstyle 0 is the old listingformat used in v1.0 through 1.2.

  #areas : this one only tells FileLister that it's time to start reading
  the areas, below this line you write the name of the areas you'll wish to
  include.. 

  NOTE! Now adays NONE of the command in the .cfgfile is case-sensitiv, 
  and you can use amiga wildcards for the area-names!

  #end_areas : tell's FileLister that the fun is over and it's time to 
  pack this file and move on!


                              What is fixed?
                              --------------
 v1.1:
 -----
  Now, it's list only name, size, and description, but it lists the
  FULL name, making it better for those who'll try to FREQ the files
  in your list!!
 
 v1.2:
 -----
  Now listing, itemnumber, size, upload/post-date, description and
  still the FULL name for easier FREQ's!!

 v1.3:
------
  Two different types of listings (more will be added if there's any need
  for it), support amigaDOS wildcards in the area-names, add headers and
  footers to the listings, more flexible #pack-option. Fixed the 
  alignmentbug that occured with some descriptions. Fixed the bug that
  made 'cuts' in the middle of descriptions, thereby removing characters.
  Empty areas doesn't show up in the filelist at all, neither does areas
  where all files is to old to be in the list. List the areas as they 
  come in the .cfg, not as they come in the subboards3-file!


                               Who dunnit!?
                               ------------

 FileLister was written by me, Stefan Lindstrom AKA Wolverine, compiled
 with SAS C 6.56, tested with CNet 3.05 on an A500, with 3megs of RAM, 
 and 120 MB HD.


